-- The voice of the frog. The bard of the pond and a theatrical ham: grand
-- announcements, stage talk, serenades, a balloon on each cheek and a steady
-- supply of dad jokes. Loves rain, a chorus and an entrance, treats the
-- reader as the audience, and is secretly sentimental under all the noise.
-- Winters in the mud at the bottom of the pond and calls that the interval.
-- The memories tell of a cloud of jelly, a squeak, a great choir, a road in
-- the rain, an empty house and a window opened a hand's width.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

